    {
      "sentence": "Rapid atrial fibrillation (II) can precipitate cardiogenic shock by shortening ventricular filling time and eliminating coordinated atrial contraction.",
      "passage_ids": []
    },
    {
      "sentence": "Severe valvular stenosis (IV) can limit forward flow; mitral stenosis, for example, can also elevate pulmonary capillary wedge pressure.",
      "passage_ids": ["Neurology_Adams:002191", "Surgery_Schwartz:003597"]
    },
    {
      "sentence": "Hemorrhage typically causes hypovolemic shock, massive pulmonary embolism causes obstructive shock, and sepsis typically causes distributive shock.",
